From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:12:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Paint corner-shape on backgrounds and clips

Stylo computes corner-*-shape, but every box path was built from
elliptical arcs, so a bevel, scoop, notch or squircle corner painted
round. When a visible corner is shaped, the border-box, padding-box and
content-box paths and the shadow clip now come from a superellipse
contour ported from WPT's render-corner-shape.js reference, which
follows Blink: the inner edges move along the same approximate normal
the reference uses, so test and reference agree. Boxes with only round
corners keep their arc paths unchanged.
